    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1254">

                <pb facs="1007" n="891" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg891"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.2311/31.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                    Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-09T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 9, 1912—7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The following telegram has been sent to the Governor of Texas: (See supra.)</p>
                <p>Accordingly you will immediately cancel the permission, pending further
                    instructions, to be based on your report as to a stipulation that the troops
                    will be used exclusively to preserve order at Juárez.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
